    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Before the exam: topical anesthetic (eg, proparacaine 0.5% 1–2 drops) into the inferior fornix."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Corneal abrasion (incl after rust-ring removal): ophthalmic antibiotic ointment (eg, bacitracin/polymyxin B or erythromycin) until healed; contact lens wearers: antipseudomonal (eg, ciprofloxacin 0.3% ointment)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Ophthalmic corticosteroids are contraindicated (fungal growth, HSV reactivation)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Suspected globe laceration, before the ophthalmologist: IV antibiotics (eg, ceftazidime and vancomycin); tetanus prophylaxis for open globe injuries."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
